# Program 14: Student Application Using Express.js

## Aim

To create an Express application with routes, GET and POST requests, middleware, static files, and a template engine.

This program uses **EJS** as the template engine.

## Step 1: Install Packages

Initialize the Node.js project and install Express.js and EJS.

```bash
npm init -y
npm install express ejs
```

## Step 2: Create Folder Structure

Create the following files and folders:

```text
studentapp/
├── app.js
├── public/
│   └── style.css
└── views/
    └── students.ejs
```

## Step 3: Write the Code in `app.js`

```javascript
var express = require('express');
var app = express();

app.set('view engine', 'ejs');
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));

// Middleware
app.use(function(req, res, next) {
    console.log(req.method, req.url);
    next();
});

// Static files
app.use(express.static('public'));

// Home route
app.get('/', function(req, res) {
    res.send('<h1>Welcome to Student Application</h1>');
});

// About route
app.get('/about', function(req, res) {
    res.send('About Student Application');
});

// Students page
app.get('/students', function(req, res) {
    res.render('students', { name: 'Ravi', roll: 101 });
});

// POST request
app.post('/students', function(req, res) {
    res.send('Student details submitted successfully');
});

app.listen(3000, function() {
    console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

## Step 4: Write the Code in `views/students.ejs`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Student Details</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Student Details</h1>
    <p>Name: <%= name %></p>
    <p>Roll Number: <%= roll %></p>
</body>
</html>
```

## Step 5: Write the Code in `public/style.css`

```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background-color: lightblue;
}
```

## Step 6: Run the Application

Start the server using:

```bash
node app.js
```

The terminal displays:

```text
Server running on port 3000
```

## Step 7: Test the Application

Open your browser and visit the following URLs:

| URL                              | Description                        |
| -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `http://localhost:3000/`         | Displays the welcome message       |
| `http://localhost:3000/about`    | Displays the about page            |
| `http://localhost:3000/students` | Displays student details using EJS |

The POST route `/students` can be tested using a form or an API testing tool.

## Output

**Home Page:**

```text
Welcome to Student Application
```

**About Page:**

```text
About Student Application
```

**Students Page:**

```text
Student Details

Name: Ravi
Roll Number: 101
```

The students page has a light blue background.

## Result

Thus, an Express.js student application was created successfully using routes, GET and POST requests, middleware, static files, and the EJS template engine.
